  "content": {
    "id": "p22-p1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Consider $f(x)=(x-1)(x+2)(x-3)$. Determine when $f(x)\\leq 0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x\\leq -2$ or $1\\leq x\\leq 3$.",
      "worked": "The zeroes are $-2$, $1$ and $3$. Each has multiplicity one, so the sign changes at each zero. Testing one value in each interval gives:\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(-3)&=-24<0\\\\f(0)&=6>0\\\\f(2)&=-4<0\\\\f(4)&=18>0\\end{aligned}$$\nInclude the zeroes because the inequality is non-strict. Hence $x\\leq -2$ or $1\\leq x\\leq 3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 26
  },
